Campfire for BEAM: wallet-api --privileged_shader_sha256=<hex>[,<hex>...]

Stock wallet-api runs every app shader at privilege 0 (api_cli.cpp:340). Shaders
that derive keys from the master KDF (get_PkEx, get_BlindSk, SetKernelAdv; e.g.
BANS "user view" and "receive_all") fail there. Granting privilege 1 to every shader
would let any dApp derive keys other dApps use, so only shaders whose SHA-256 of the
exact `contract` bytes is listed get a privilege-1 manager; all others keep the
stock privilege-0 manager. Empty list (the default) = stock behaviour.

Also: process_invoke_data refuses invoke data that asks to re-run an app body at a
privilege above 0 unless this process compiled that body from an allowlisted shader
(never above 1). Stock honours whatever privilege the client-supplied data names
(contract_transaction.cpp:648). Invoke data wallet-api itself produced at privilege 0
is unaffected.

Applies after 0001-bind-loopback.patch, to tag beam-7.5.14493, with patch -p1.

